<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How East Germany boosted Vietnam's coffee industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2de3aa78f1f8741456fdc1738412d6b790c249058835a98e6c1925eae394e68b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974--4f080bc8669e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When East Germany could no longer afford to import coffee, it introduced a substitute blend containing rye and chicory in 1977. A public outcry ensued. The solution to the problem lay 9,000 kilometers away — in Vietnam.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>France seeks German man in Channel migrant boat probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8013375be0bb9f73bb4fd7de1ba1d47d8370f687b588a3c4de3cae5e12b61733</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069--841769bf9248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German businessman is accused of supplying equipment to smugglers organizing migrant crossings from France to the United Kingdom. However, he can't face formal charges until he is extradited to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trial of Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia begins after delay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:379977ea21f46df5045d59230af7eb2f04f5adb5d850129a5f9c732319ce6c05</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677--743246431230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite delays due to health issues, the trial of the Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia has begun. Prosecutors say the defendant used her military contacts to provide information on German defense and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: IG Metall union says deal reached with employers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f79af0046ef19a5abe1fa59c8afa8129da204d580820ab5abe369fd2dd30e580</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792--f4aca602c9d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IG Metall, representing millions of workers in Germany's metal and electrical industry, is the country's largest trade union. The deal came after more than 24 hours of talks with employers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Cologne court awards record damages in Catholic sex abuse case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69344e0c98b35f32484c22b28d516ec459ed5572b92037cd65d0faf02758f4c6</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746--18122980124b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court has awarded the highest damages ever in Germany to a victim of sexual abuse linked to the Catholic Church. An alleged spy and suspected terrorists are also making headlines in Germany on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: 2 arrested, suspected of plotting synagogue attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b75c71fd02432212a4d7609644473f58440476e56df3a27d8a674f5499b120d7</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715--3c7a6577a7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Federal prosecutors say they have ordered the arrest of two members of a pro-Iranian group on suspicion of planning an attack on a synagogue. They were detained in the cities of Heidelberg and Cologne.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The tiny BSW is a party in crisis, as it is set to hand the far-right AfD power in eastern Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:148186c923b5d55c28665ee4eddcf690965cce0f6cdc76118170d2f234e9e387</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417--98b542aa0047.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sahra Wagenknecht's BSW party is set to disrupt German politics yet again. Espousing a mix of left-wing economic policy and populist far-right anti-migration rhetoric, it now stands to play kingmaker to the far right AfD</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Indian workers fill Germany's labor gaps but face hurdles and risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73e181bea48f68ed0ef89936b4ece7bc7d7ee0e1beca8e48a582889ed690fb91</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882--78ecce9504e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of Indians working in Germany has grown rapidly in recent years. But many continue to face challenges in the labor market. Some also fall victim to recruitment scams, leaving them vulnerable to exploitation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German Catholic Church abuse victims may receive higher compensation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c56733ae9d4dbc63a0584057d468935754a6c3970cd810dad9bf5876ab50cd3</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T10:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-catholic-church-abuse-victims-may-receive-higher-compensation/a-80071917--9cefa7338ff2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-catholic-church-abuse-victims-may-receive-higher-compensation/a-80071917?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a landmark ruling, judges in Cologne found the Catholic Church responsible for abuse committed by clergy members. Victims could now be entitled to more compensation.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>On farewell trip, Steinmeier calls for more investment in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72af0cfb9b525a2ac35d43146076b26bebeb42f8a5cef1c07f282a6138aaba99</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717--a2b49bd3f417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana, Kenya: On his last trip to Africa, outgoing German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier called on companies at home to be bolder and seize opportunities in Africa.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6dcac703ee114ca2c514fd6c279d73bdb58614773c4b69b94d89e123100b74</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
